
:PRONOUN

; The speaker and the one he speaks to, each case tagged: the realizer says "I" where he is the
; subject, "me" where he is not, "my" in place of a possessor ("my home"; morphology.mmorph
; possessive:). An untagged form serves every case no tagged one does.
"I"        ?_I     :: case:subject     .
"me"       ?_I     :: case:object      .
"my"       ?_I     :: case:possessive  .
"mine"     ?_I     .
"myself"   ?_I     :: case:reflexive   .
"you"      ?_you   .
"your"     ?_you   :: case:possessive  .
"yourself" ?_you   :: case:reflexive   .
"this"     ?_this  .

; Third-person pronouns, one variable per gender and case: ?_third_m he, ?_third_mo him,
; ?_third_f she, ?_third_fo her, ?_third_s they, ?_third_o them (the default for a referent of
; unknown gender). The realize layer picks the variable by the referent's gender; a player's
; pronoun binds the man the NPC's talk gives it, of that gender.

"she"   ?_third_f   :: agree:f  .
"he"    ?_third_m   :: agree:m  .
"they"  ?_third_s   :: agree:pl .

"her"   ?_third_fo   :: agree:f  .
"him"   ?_third_mo   :: agree:m  .
"them"  ?_third_o   :: agree:pl .
